Today, we visited the [Enoggera State School YMCA](https://www.facebook.com/pages/Enoggera-State-Primary-school/161763917183424) north of Brisbane for a school holiday incursion! We also visited them last holidays for a Drum Sing Dance Workshop but this time we were just DANCING  and what a fabulous group AGAIN! We had loads of activities and dancing fun! The wonderful group of children who absolutely loved dancing African moves to the groovy Sidiki Diabate African Pop King! and of course the YMCA staff that did exceptionally well in the dance moves! We danced Djole & Macru rhythms and of course had some super special time when all of the groups got up performed their self choreographed dance routines! Thanks for having us Enoggera... we look forward to seeing you all again!!
